@page "/privacy-policy"
@inherits SitePage

@* Legacy PrivacyPolicy/Index, with its two placeholder sections (1 and 6) written, the date updated and links to My Account, the contact page and the cookie policy. *@

<SeoHead Page="Page" PageName="Privacy Policy" Keywords="privacy policy, data protection, personal information, travel privacy"
         MetaDescription="At Fuse Hostels and Travels, we take your privacy seriously. Our privacy policy outlines how we protect and handle your personal information when you book with us." />

<LegalPage Id="privacyPolicy" Title="@(Page is null ? "PRIVACY POLICY" : PageHeadings.Of(Page, "PRIVACY POLICY").Title)">
        <p>Last updated: 25 September 2026</p>
        <h5>
            Our Commitment
        </h5>
        <p>
            Fuse Hostels and Travel (herein referred to as “Fuse Hostels and Travel”, “we”, “us” or “our”) is dedicated to secure and protect your data privacy rights, and to guarantee that all personal data collected from customers are managed pursuant to the principles of genuine business purpose and transparency to maintain your privacy online.
        </p>
        <h5>
            1. Who are we?
        </h5>
        <p>
            Fuse Hostels and Travel runs hostels and tours in Vietnam, and this website (fusehostelsandtravel.com). We decide how and why your personal information is used when you book with us, stay with us, create an account or contact us, which makes us responsible for it. Our contact details are in section 9 below.
        </p>
        <h5>
            2. What we may collect from you?
        </h5>
        <p>
            We will collect your personal information when you make a booking with us or use Fuse Hostels and Travel websites and mobile applications. Such information may include, among others:
        </p>
        <p>
            Your name;<br />
            Address;<br />
            Birthdate;<br />
            Gender;<br />
            Contact details (including your email address and telephone/mobile number;<br />
            Government ID details;<br />
            Details of your external accounts (Facebook, Twitter, Google);<br />
            Credit card details via a reputable partner listed on the payment pages<br />
            Country; and<br />
            Such other information as we may collect with your consent or as required by law.
        </p>
        <h5>3. How we use your information</h5>
        <p>
            Approve, facilitate, administer and process your booking;<br />
            Respond to queries, requests and complaints and improve how we interact with you;<br />
            Send you statements, billings, notices and other such documents necessary for continued use of our services;<br />
            Conduct studies and researches for the purpose of reviewing, developing and improving our services;<br />
            Reach out to you regarding products and services information, including offers, promotions, discounts, rewards;<br />
            Perform such other activities permitted by law or with your consent;
        </p>
        <h5>4. How we may share your information</h5>
        <p>
            We may share your personal information to the following:<br />
            To our subsidiaries, affiliates, branches, related corporations, associates, assignees, agents, commercial partners service providers and/or any other parties engaged by us to enable or assist us in the provision of services;<br />
            To companies which help us improve our business or third-party service providers which help us deliver services to you;<br />
            To comply with legal, regulatory, security and processing requirements, national and foreign governmental requirements applicable to us or our affiliates or service providers; and<br />
            To carry out all other purposes set out above.
        </p>
        <h5>
            5. How long do we keep your information?
        </h5>
        <p>
            Your personal details shall be retained by us until no longer used or useful in serving your requests or booking  and/or until such time as it is no longer necessary to keep your information for any other legal and business purposes.
        </p>
        <h5>
            6. What are the customers’ rights?
        </h5>
        <p>
            You have the right to:<br />
            Ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you (you can download most of it yourself from <a href="/my-account/personal-data">My Account</a>);<br />
            Correct information that's wrong or out of date (most of it you can update in <a href="/my-account/profile">My Account</a>);<br />
            Ask us to delete your information, or to stop or limit how we use it;<br />
            Object to us using your information for marketing, at any time; and<br />
            Withdraw any consent you've given us, without affecting what we did before you withdrew it.<br />
            To use any of these rights, contact us using the details in section 9. We'll reply within 30 days, and may ask you to confirm who you are first. We may need to keep some information, such as booking and payment records, where the law requires it.
        </p>
        <p>
            Please note that if you communicate your objection to our use and/or disclosure of your personal information for the purposes and in the manner as stated above, depending on the nature of your objection, we may not be in a position to continue to provide our services to you or perform on any contract we have with you. Our legal rights and remedies are expressly reserved in such an event.
        </p>
        <h5>
            7. How do we protect your information?
        </h5>
        <p>
            We fully recognize the value of your personal information. Thus, we strive to maintain the confidentiality and integrity of your personal information by employing physical, technological and procedural precautions. We train our employees to properly handle your information. Whenever we engage other companies to provide services for us, we require them to protect personal information aligned with our own security standards.
        </p>
        <h5>
            8. How can I request for my data to be deleted?
        </h5>
        <p>
            As a user, you have a right to have your data deleted, and we have a responsibility to delete your data upon request. You may request this by contacting our customer service team through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or at info@fusehostelsandtravel.com.
        </p>
        <h5>9. How to contact us?</h5>
        <p>
            Should you have questions regarding our privacy statement, about how your personal information is used, or about how to exercise your right of access, rectification, or objection under the Data Privacy Laws, you can contact us directly at the business address or e-mail address below:
        </p>
        <p>
            Fuse Hostels and Travel<br />
            25 Nguyễn Phan Vinh<br />
            Hội An, Quảng Nam<br />
            Cẩm An, Vietnam
        </p>
        <p> Email: info@fusehostelsandtravel.com</p>
        <h5>Cookies</h5>
        <p>Fuse Hostels &amp; Travel uses cookie in our web pages to:</p>
        <p>
            Maintain your session and required details during the booking process (session cookie)<br />
            Collect website and mobile application usage data for statistical/analytic purposes (analytics cookie)<br />
            Directing you to the correct landing page based on your geo-location (geo-targeting cookie)<br />
            Provide analytics and user experience data<br />
            You may instruct your browser, by changing its settings, to stop accepting cookies or to prompt you before accepting a cookie from the websites or application that you visit. Fuse Hostel &amp; Travel website and application may not function properly if cookie setting is disabled. Learn more in our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.
        </p>
</LegalPage>

@code {
    protected override DefaultIdType PageId => SitePages.PrivacyPolicy;
}
